turkey is set to open a new chapter in  its european union membership  negotiations the first time it's done so  in three years at a meeting in  Luxembourg de use general affairs  council decided the talks could begin on  regional policy and the coordination of  structural instruments this is one of 35  policy areas or chapters that all  aspiring EU candidates must comply with  to join the negotiations will be  launched in Brussels on the fifth of  November turkey began its membership  talks in 2005 it's so far opened 14  chapters I hope we'll catch up I'll  continue so an important the deliverable  after three years and let's hope it will  be really good basis for the  continuation The ministers also discuss  preparations for the European Council of  heads of state and government in two  days key items on the summit agenda  include the completion of the digital  single market combating youth  unemployment improved access to finances  for small and medium-sized businesses as  well as strengthening policies that  underpin the Euro single currency and  completing the banking Union  preparations for the Eastern Partnership  summit in Lithuania at the end of next  month and the plight of asylum seekers  tried across the Mediterranean to Europe  are also up for discussion the ministers  also endorsed a report on the European  semester process which helps member  states to better organize their budgets  and economic policies they agreed that  the process which concluded in July was  largely successful but that some  shortcomings still need to be addressed
 

